[10181]="70016B87\n1\tDefeat Istash\tIstash is at Uruk-gashan, south of Mekhem-bizru. Haflith believes Durin's Stone will never be safe until Istash, an Orc-leader, is defeated.\n2\tTalk to Haflith at Mekhem-bizru\tHaflith is at Mekhem-bizru, north of Uruk-gashan. Haflith will be pleased to hear Istash has been defeated, and Durin's Stone remains safe.\n",
[10182]="7000EC64\n1\tCollect slabs of troll-stone (total: 10)\tSun-touched trolls can be found throughout the Ettenmoors. Forzunk ordered you to collect slabs of troll-stone for the war-effort.\n2\tBring the troll-stone to Forzunk at Gramsfoot\t\n",
[10183]="7005B444\n1\tDefeat Wargs (total: 12)\tWargs can be found in western Clovengap. Gunvald has asked for your assistance in thinning the Warg packs in Clovengap.\n2\tReturn to Gunvald\tGunvald is in a camp in the south-western area of Clovengap. You should let Gunvald know you have culled the Warg population of Clovengap.\n",
[10184]="70050B1A\n1\tThere is much work to be done, if the Zhélruka hope to settle in the formidable Grey Mountains.\t\n2\tAssist the Zhélruka (total: 10)\tLend a hand in Skarháld by assisting Stráhek the Stout and by completing Wanted Pebbles quests. Completing this quest will unlock Reclaiming the Grey II, and can be replayed weekly.\n",
[10185]="70050B38\n1\tAssist the Zhélruka (total: 10)\tLend a hand in Skarháld by assisting Stráhek the Stout and by completing Wanted Pebbles quests. Completing this quest will unlock Reclaiming the Grey III, and can be replayed weekly. This quest will be removed on the weekly reset time, and so must be completed weekly by that time.\n",
[10186]="70050B37\n1\tAssist the Zhélruka (total: 10)\tLend a hand in Skarháld by assisting Stráhek the Stout and by completing Wanted Pebbles quests. This quest will be removed on the weekly reset time, and so must be completed weekly by that time.\n",
[10187]="7000E5BD\n1\tFëoc is at Voi-teltta, west of Ida's camp along the road. Ida has charged you with defeating the Gauradan Fëoc, who has claimed Voi-teltta for himself and driven out the Lossoth scouts.\t\n2\tTalk to Ida\tIda is at her encampment, east of Voi-teltta near the entrance to the ice canyons that lead south. You have reclaimed Voi-teltta for the Lossoth. You should return to Ida and tell her of your success.\n3\tTalk to Scout-master Lauri\tLauri is at Pynti-peldot, atop a hill north and west along the road from Ida's camp. Ida has asked that you inform Lauri of your reclamation of the Voi-teltta homestead.\n",
[10188]="7005A689\n1\tComplete Gundabad: Reclaiming the Mountain-hold quests (total: 20)\tGundabad: Reclaiming the Mountain-hold quests are available from Zádokh Flint-eye, Agátur the Boastful, and Bráthi at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset. You should talk to these dwarves as soon as you are able.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted many Gundabad: Reclaiming the Mountain-hold quests assisting in Reclaiming the Mountain-hold.\n",
[10189]="7001542B\n1\tDefeat enemies or creatures at Menem-berej (total: 12)\tMenem-berej is just south of the central miners' camp in the Silvertine Lodes. You should clear the platform and its surrounding area of any dangerous creatures.\n2\tReturn to Thalfar\tThalfar is in the central mining camp the Silvertine Lodes. You should return to Thalfar and inform him that the platform has been cleared, for now.\n",
[10190]="7000700E\n1\tCollect Earth-kin weapons (total: 8)\tThe stolen weapons may be found on hostile Rauta-lehmä Earth-kin in Nan Amlug, east of Rusfold. You should recover stolen weapons from the hostile Earth-kin, and return them to Iivari at Rusfold.\n2\tReturn the Earth-kin weapons to Iivari\tIivari is at Rusfold. You should bring the recovered weapons to Iivari.\n",
[10191]="700265E1\n1\tTalk to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë is at Tinnudir, north of Annúminas. You have been instructed to speak with Orchalwë.\n",
[10192]="700078B1\n1\tTalk to Constable Wren\tConstable Wren is at the guard-house, east of Combe. Maida Woodwright has asked that you speak with Constable Wren regarding the whereabouts of her son, Covell.\n2\tTalk to Covell Woodwright\tCovell may be found at one of the Blackwold camps north and east of the Combe lumber camp. Maida Woodwright sent you to speak with Constable Wren, who suggested that Covell joined the Blackwolds and would likely be found near one of their camps in the Chetwood.\n3\tTalk to Constable Wren\tConstable Wren patrols near the guard-house on the hill south of the lumber camp and east of Combe. You discovered Covell Woodwright on the path leading through the Chetwood, and he attacked you. Though you defeated him, he escaped deeper into the woods. Constable Wren will want to hear of your encounter with the brigand.\n4\tTalk to Maida Woodwright\tMaida Woodwright is back in Combe. Maida Woodwright must be told that her son Covell has joined the Blackwold brigands.\n",
[10193]="700687B8\n1\tTalk to Imêna at The Din of Arms\030Talk to Nûr at the Dahâl Huliz\030Talk to Sophân at the Gate of Steps\tJihan has tasked you with interviewing three individuals in the Tor-gardens. Imêna works at The Din of Arms to the south-west. Sophân waits by the Gate of Steps to the south. Nûr can be found to the south-east outside the Dahâl Huliz.\n2\tTalk to Jihan in the gardens\tYou have finished interviewing all three people and taken notes. You should bring the notes to Jihan in the gardens outside Dâr Tabib.\n",
[10194]="70016B32\n1\tTalk to Arnod at the gardens of Tharâkh Bazân\tArnod is camped at Tharâkh Bazân in Durin's Way. Búkk is interested in tales of the battles that the dwarves lost to the Orcs. He believes Moria still holds these secrets and that Arnod may know where to find them.\n2\tCollect records (total: 4)\tThe pages are located in the chambers to the north and south of Salab Nurjundul, west of Jazârgund. Arnod believes the old tales are still in Moria.\n3\tTalk to Arnod at Tharâkh Bazân\tArnod is camped at Tharâkh Bazân, west from Jazârgund. Arnod wants to help in understanding the history behind the tales you found.\n",
[10195]="7005A41D\n1\tCollect dwarf-helmets (total: 4)\030Collect dwarf-shields (total: 8)\030Collect dwarf-swords (total: 10)\tFallen dwarves are strewn across the field near Durin's Stone. You should retrieve arms and armour from the fallen.\n2\tReturn to Dráttur\tDráttur is located in Amdân. Bring the arms and armour to Dráttur.\n",
[10196]="70009A5C\n1\tFind the lost leaf of paper\tRonald Dwale remembers dropping his paper somewhere in Dwaling, north of the Bullroarer's Sward. Ronald Dwale has asked you to find his lost leaf of paper.\n2\tTalk to Ronald Dwale\tRonald Dwale is at Hob Hillbrow's home at the Bullroarer's Sward in Dwaling. You should return the leaf of paper to Ronald Dwale.\n",
[10197]="70067C4B\n1\tFind the ravaged caravan\tThe guard's report suggested that the caravan was ambushed by the Haradrim while travelling the south road. Search along the road for signs of the ambushed caravan.\n2\tCollect the caravan manifest\tYou have discovered the caravan. It was clearly ambushed, the cargo stolen, and all occupants are missing. You should set about finding the manifest.\n3\tReturn the items to Girgish at the crest of Jax Phanâl\030Recover food crates ([see journal]/8)\030Recover the ornate cruet\030Recover the sealed document case\030Recover ornate weapons ([see journal]/12)\tThe manifest lists the items aboard as eight crates of food, an ornate cruet meant as a gift, a sealed document case, and twelve ornate weapons. Perhaps the Haradrim have them within their camp to the east. You should venture there in search of these items.\n",
[10198]="7006C133\n1\tRecover stolen historical scrolls (total: 8)\030Recover stolen historical artifacts (total: 6)\030Defeat All-seeing cultists (total: 12)\tDefeat All-seeing cultists and recover historical artifacts and documents.\n2\tSearch for the Barkhûshim leader Katrakhi Mâta near the centre of Dûl Zidur\tSearch for the Barkhûshim leader Katrakhi Mâta near the centre of Dûl Zidur.\n3\tDefeat Katrakhi Mâta\tDefeat Katrakhi Mâta!\n",
[10199]="70072EF8\n1\tExamine the parchments strewn upon the barrel near the entrance of Drushkála\tZaumoz the Black Wind, captain of the ship Grishúlvosh, has invited Orcs of Drushkála to join his crew.\n2\tYou should search for slain Orcs in Drushkála to see what you can learn of the Grishúlvosh's crew.\t\n3\tCompleted\tThe Grishúlvosh must now have at least four new crew members.\n",
[10200]="7004AB9E\n1\tComplete The Burning Mountain: Red Skies\tCandúr can be found in Udûn. You should talk Candúr.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted The Burning Mountain: Red Skies.\n",
[10201]="700280A5\n1\tTalk to Knotfist\tDelwin wants you to speak with Knotfist and stop the violence.\n2\tTalk to Delwin\tHaving heard from the Abomination leader, Knotfist, speak again with Delwin.\n3\tTalk to Delwin\tSpeak with Delwin outside Lhan Colvarn.\n",
[10202]="700265BD\n1\tRemove the corpses from the cages (total: 6)\tThe corpses should be removed from the crow's cages to allow the fallen to rest peacefully.\n2\tTalk to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë will be pleased to see his dishonoured brethren will now rest peacefully.\n",
[10203]="70020DC4\n1\tTBD\t\n2\tTBD\t\n",
[10204]="70020DC1\n1\tDefeat bugan (total: 12)\tKhoblún Utot lies to the south of Maur Tulhau. Iolo Brochtû has asked you to return to Khoblún Utot and drive out the bugan.\n2\tTalk to Iolo Brochtû at Maur Tulhau\tIolo Brochtû is at Maur Tulhau, north of Khoblún Utot. You should return to Iolo Brochtû with news of your success.\n",
[10205]="700160EE\n1\tSpeak with Simbi at the Twenty-first Hall\tSimbi is in the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You should tell Simbi of your restoration of the lighting system in Zelem-melek.\n",
[10206]="700160EA\n1\tTalk to Thórgnyr in Anazârmekhem\tThórgnyr is in Anazârmekhem, north of The Cross-roads of Ash. Thórgnyr will want to know that you re-aligned the mirror.\n",
[10207]="7001601E\n1\tTalk to Thettmárr at the Deep Descent\tThettmárr is in the Deep Descent. You should tell Thettmárr of your continuing efforts towards making Khazad-dûm safe once more.\n",
[10208]="70016022\n1\tSpeak to a Guard at the East Gate of Moria in Nud-melek\tDwarves hold the East Gate of Moria in Nud-melek. You should tell a guard of your continuing efforts towards lighting Khazad-dûm once more.\n",
